\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces DEPT in front of a protected NIDS. The packet-to-tensor pipeline derives two views of each flow: bit-level packet tokens for the TCN and prefix statistics for the Random Forest. The meta-learner fuses the two prediction streams into a verdict at every packet. Unflagged flows pass unchanged; flagged flows are corrected by the reconstructor and realized back into packets, so the NIDS receives traffic, not tensors.}}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{4}{DEPT in front of a protected NIDS. The packet-to-tensor pipeline derives two views of each flow: bit-level packet tokens for the TCN and prefix statistics for the Random Forest. The meta-learner fuses the two prediction streams into a verdict at every packet. Unflagged flows pass unchanged; flagged flows are corrected by the reconstructor and realized back into packets, so the NIDS receives traffic, not tensors}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]4}{}{}{}}
